Day 10 of hashtag#60DayClaudeChallenge ✅
Built my personal portfolio website today — entirely with Claude, no manual coding.
One thing I learned about personal branding while building it: your portfolio isn't just a list of skills, it's proof. Instead of saying "I know SQL and Excel," I can now showcase projects I've actually built—Nutra Scope, a Sales Dashboard, and an India AQI Dashboard. Recruiters don't have to rely on claims; they can see my work and the problems I've solved.
It also made me rethink how I describe my work. Turning resume bullet points into a story that's easy to scan in 10 seconds is a skill in itself.
I'd love to hear from the community and hiring teams:
What is the first thing you look for in a candidate's portfolio? Any feedback or suggestions to make mine better would be greatly appreciated!
